## Hooks

Bobby scaffolds two Claude Code hooks that protect against context loss and missing learnings:

- **PreCompact** (`hooks/precompact.sh`) — fires before Claude compresses context. Prompts you to write a `progress.md` checkpoint in the ticket folder so work can resume after compaction without losing your place.
- **Stop** (`hooks/stop.sh`) — fires every `BOBBY_SAVE_INTERVAL` turns (default 20) before stopping. Prompts you to record any new anti-patterns or validated approaches via `bobby learn` before the session ends.

Set `BOBBY_SAVE_INTERVAL` in your shell environment to change the frequency.
<% } -%>

## Architecture Wakeup

All agents should load `.bobby/architecture-wakeup.md` (if it exists) as part of their "Before Starting" step. This compressed summary (~300 tokens) gives agents shared context about the codebase without loading the full `architecture.md`.

Run `bobby run arch` to generate or regenerate these files after major refactors.

## Learnings

Each skill has a `learnings.md` file that accumulates anti-patterns. Always check learnings before starting work. Also check `<%= paths.skills %>/bobby-shared/learnings.md` — it holds cross-agent patterns that apply to all agents.

## Bobby CLI Commands

```
bobby ticket create -t "Title" --type bug -p high   # Create ticket
bobby ticket create -t "Epic" --epic                # Create epic (breaks down)
bobby run define TKT-001                            # Product definition: brief → personas → journeys → features → blueprint
bobby blueprint                                     # See the whole plan on one page before building
bobby ticket list                                   # Show board
bobby ticket list --blocked                         # Show blocked tickets
bobby ticket view TKT-001                           # View ticket
bobby ticket view TKT-001 --plan                    # View plan
bobby ticket move TKT-001 review                   # Move to reviewing
bobby ticket move TKT-001 reject "reason"          # Reject back to building
bobby ticket move TKT-001 block "reason"           # Block ticket
bobby ticket move TKT-001 unblock                  # Unblock ticket
bobby run next TKT-001                      # Slow mode: next agent for stage
bobby run workflow TKT-001                  # Fast mode: auto-chain all agents
bobby run plan                              # Batch: plan all tickets in planning
bobby run ship                              # Ship all ready tickets
bobby run arch                              # Discover + document architecture (wakeup + decisions)
bobby run intake                            # Convert pasted PM spec → ticket
bobby run ux                                # Freeform UX design review
bobby run pm                                # Freeform PM product review
bobby run security TKT-001                  # Security audit (OWASP + STRIDE)
bobby run debug TKT-001                     # Root-cause debugging
bobby run docs                              # Update docs after shipping
bobby run performance                              # Performance benchmarking
bobby run watchdog                            # Post-deploy health check
bobby retro TKT-001 "pattern"              # Create retrospective
bobby retro --weekly                        # Weekly retro with metrics
bobby learn bobby-build "pattern" "desc"    # Add learning
bobby upgrade                               # Upgrade Bobby to latest version
```
## Shipped vs yours

Every file Bobby scaffolds follows one rule:

| Shipped — replaced on upgrade | Yours — never overwritten |
|---|---|
| `<%= paths.skills %>/<skill>/SKILL.md` | `<%= paths.skills %>/<skill>/SKILL.local.md` |
| `<%= paths.skills %>/<skill>/learnings.md` | `<%= paths.skills %>/<skill>/learnings.local.md` |
| `<%= paths.agents %>/<agent>.md` | `<%= paths.agents %>/<agent>.local.md` |
| everything above `<!-- bobby:end -->` in this file | everything below it, and `CLAUDE.local.md` |

**Wherever you read a Bobby file `X.ext`, also read `X.local.ext` if it exists — and let it
win.** Put project-specific instructions in the `.local` file; anything written into a shipped
file is lost on the next upgrade.


